      "id": "cibal-i-sugure",
      "end": 1599,
      "contributors": [],
      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p><em>Nehr-i S\u016bs</em><span>:\u00a0It flows above the city called\u00a0</span><em>\u0130stanca</em><span>\u00a0(Istanja / \u00c9cija, Spain).\u00a0The inhabitants of the villages along its banks engage in abundant agriculture.\u00a0It descends from the\u00a0</span><em>cib\u0101l-i \u015eu\u0121\u016bre</em><span>\u00a0(Mountains of Shughur / Sierra Morena) toward\u00a0</span><em>C\u00fchel\u0101cin\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(J\u016bhala\u2013Cin\u0101n? a region in al-Andalus), then passes by the cities of\u00a0</span><em>Yeb\u0101t</em><span>\u00a0(\u00c9bora / Evora?) and\u00a0</span><em>\u1e32ur\u1e6duba</em><span>\u00a0(C\u00f3rdoba).\u00a0To the east, it reaches\u00a0</span><em>\u0130\u015fbiliyye</em><span>\u00a0(Seville); to the west, it passes by\u00a0</span><em>\u1e6c\u0131rm\u0101na</em><span>\u00a0(Tirmana?) and finally flows into the\u00a0</span><em>Ba\u1e25r-i Mu\u1e25\u012b\u1e6d</em><span>\u00a0(the Atlantic Ocean).\u00a0In this river, just as in the\u00a0</span><em>Dicle</em><span>\u00a0(Tigris) near Basra, tides (</span><em>medd u cezr</em><span>) occur.\u00a0It is said that during the tidal period, the water advances seventy miles, and even then its water does not become salty, but remains fresh.\u00a0The more the moon\u2019s light increases, the greater the rising tide becomes.\u00a0Ships set out for their destinations at this favorable moment.\u00a0Sometimes, Frankish ships enter this river from the\u00a0</span><em>Ba\u1e25r-i Mu\u1e25\u012b\u1e6d</em><span>\u00a0(Atlantic) and sail as far as\u00a0</span><em>\u0130\u015fbiliyye</em><span>\u00a0(Seville). [translation]</span></p>",
